  "marks": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 100,
        "y": 1900,
        "text": "R9 wood-silk  PURPOSE: the dangler, and the predators together. Silk hangs from the canopy into the light"
      },
      {
        "x": 500,
        "y": 2100,
        "text": "1. THE DANGLER ALONE: W-s1 over a knob on a safe floor; it drops on the spot she has to stand on to cut"
      },
      {
        "x": 500,
        "y": 2140,
        "text": "the thread shows first: step back, let it drop, cut it while it hangs; or cut the flame from a jump"
      },
      {
        "x": 1300,
        "y": 1850,
        "text": "2. OVER A THROW LINE: W-s2's throw up onto the root shelf passes dang-s2's silk: wait out its drop, then go"
      },
      { "x": 1830, "y": 2840, "text": "the slow line under the shelf: a dark dip with root steps" },
      {
        "x": 2400,
        "y": 2050,
        "text": "3. THE COMPOSITION: burr-silk in the light's pool, dang-s3 over the only cut spot (the knob), one wick: one snuff sends both"
      },
      {
        "x": 2980,
        "y": 2500,
        "text": "burr-silk is fenced east of the flame (3054-3186, 186 past it), clear of the knob's landing: land, then snuff, not a duel"
      },
      {
        "x": 3300,
        "y": 2400,
        "text": "the dark half: the second firefly sign (a half-hung string of glow-caps)"
      },
      {
        "x": 3150,
        "y": 2700,
        "text": "THE DEAD END: a bark floor like R4's: down-cuts break it and drop her into the roots"
      },
      { "x": 800, "y": 1700, "text": "LANDMARK: the silk hall, threads hanging into the three lights" },
      {
        "x": 300,
        "y": 1840,
        "text": "POSTGAME: W-dj on a ledge hung from the canopy on a slick root, 724 over the floor (double jump)"
      }
    ],
